* ''The vessel pins the floor'' (operator, 2026-11-11: //"The pull/push tension can go the way the memegraph/code leans"//). A release gets cut and published; each VESSEL accepts it, one pin per (vessel, Nexus) in its control home, and faces pin nothing. The accept fast-forwards along `prior` and refuses a fork or a non-descendant by name; an island that swaps its floor live swaps, any other raises the reboot alert. `lares vessel floor status|accept`. Landed (`63bc695d9`, `W26` slice 5; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane#/the-vessel-pin`>>).

